# Custom rules (everything added below won't be overriden by 'Generate .gitignore File' if you use 'Update' option)


# ── Project rules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Restored on 2026-07-30. A .gitignore generator overwrote this section, and the
# working tree then offered a 15 MB binary, the upstream SDK clones and every
# working note to the first `git add -A`. Anything below the "Custom rules"
# marker above survives that generator's Update option; anything above does not.

# Build output
/feint
# The tools that `go build ./tools/...` leaves at the root. Un-ignored, they
# reach `mise run testplan` as untracked paths no rule triages, which is a red
# with nothing behind it (#564).
/testplan
/dist/

# Upstream SDK checkouts read by the drift scan (cloned by `mise run upstream:sync`)
/.upstream/

# Emulator state snapshots
*.state.json

# Working notes: audits, and the design briefs written for whoever implements a
# lot. They are honest documents, not secrets — but they address the implementer,
# they carry dates, and they cite rules by number. A reader who lands on one from
# a search engine learns the wrong thing about what this project is. docs/ is for
# the reader; this is for the desk.
/notes/

# Agent tooling and its briefing. Published once, withdrawn deliberately: they
# address an assistant working on this repository, not somebody reading or using
# it, and a contributor should meet CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/architecture.md
# instead. Ignored rather than merely deleted, so a later session cannot put them
# back by accident.
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md

# Terraform working files. Two fixtures run terraform in this tree — the
# conformance one under tools/conformance/, and the host installer under
# tools/install/ — and both leave the same four things behind:
#
#   .terraform/     the downloaded providers. 45 MB in this repository the day
#                   this rule was written, one of them a provider binary. A
#                   `git add .` before it existed would have published all of it.
#   *.tfstate       real state. It is not secret here (the endpoints are fake and
#                   the machines are local) but a state file is never a source
#                   artefact, and the habit of committing one is what leaks the
#                   next one.
#   *.tfplan        a plan is a diff against a state, useless without it.
#   crash.log       terraform's panic dump, which carries the whole command line.
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored: it pins provider versions by
# hash, so it belongs in the repository for the same reason go.sum would.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Demo recordings. The MP4 is rebuilt by `mise run demo:network` and the tape
# itself says to keep it out of the repository.
/docs/assets/network.mp4

